# ExpressionEngine Project Structure Guide

- The main web entry points are [`index.php`](mdc:index.php) and [`admin.php`](mdc:admin.php).
- The application source lives under [`system/ee/ExpressionEngine`](mdc:system/ee/ExpressionEngine).
- The installer lives under [`system/ee/installer`](mdc:system/ee/installer).
- Public themes, assets, and control panel resources live under [`themes/ee`](mdc:themes/ee).
- User-installable templates and configuration live under [`system/user`](mdc:system/user).
- PHP Composer dependencies are vendored into [`system/ee/vendor-build`](mdc:system/ee/vendor-build) via build scripts.
- Frontend build sources for the control panel styles are in [`cp-styles/app`](mdc:cp-styles/app) with build output in [`cp-styles/build`](mdc:cp-styles/build).
- Frontend JavaScript for front editing tools lives in [`frontedit/src`](mdc:frontedit/src).
- CKEditor build sources live in [`js-src/ckeditor5-build-classic`](mdc:js-src/ckeditor5-build-classic).
- End-to-end tests live under [`tests/cypress`](mdc:tests/cypress).
- PHPUnit tests live under [`system/ee/ExpressionEngine/Tests`](mdc:system/ee/ExpressionEngine/Tests).

## Build & Scripts

- PHP dependencies are managed with Composer; see [`composer.json`](mdc:composer.json).
- Node-based tooling is managed via NPM; see root [`package.json`](mdc:package.json) and additional manifests under [`build-tools`](mdc:build-tools) and [`frontedit`](mdc:frontedit).
- Gulp/Brunch/Webpack are used to build assets; see [`gulpfile.js`](mdc:gulpfile.js) and [`webpack.config.js`](mdc:webpack.config.js).

## Development Notes

- When exploring core PHP logic, prefer starting at [`system/ee/ExpressionEngine`](mdc:system/ee/ExpressionEngine) and following namespaces/classes.
- Control panel assets that ship to `themes/ee` are built from `cp-styles` and `js-src`.